{
  "id": "john-of-the-cross-subida",
  "name": {
    "es-ES": "Subida del Monte Carmelo",
    "en-US": "The Ascent of Mount Carmel",
    "pt-BR": "Subida do Monte Carmelo"
  },
  "author": {
    "es-ES": "San Juan de la Cruz",
    "en-US": "St. John of the Cross",
    "pt-BR": "São João da Cruz"
  },
  "description": {
    "es-ES": "El primero de los grandes tratados de San Juan de la Cruz (h. 1578–1585): la noche activa del sentido y del espíritu, por la que el alma se desnuda de todo apetito y camina en pura fe, esperanza y caridad hacia la unión con Dios. Quedó sin terminar. Texto crítico del P. Silverio de Santa Teresa, con sus notas.",
    "en-US": "The first of St. John of the Cross's great treatises (c. 1578–1585): the active night of sense and spirit, in which the soul strips itself of every desire and walks in pure faith, hope and charity towards union with God. It was left unfinished. Spanish critical text of P. Silverio de Santa Teresa with his notes; English translation by David Lewis, revised by Benedict Zimmerman.",
    "pt-BR": "O primeiro dos grandes tratados de São João da Cruz (c. 1578–1585): a noite ativa do sentido e do espírito, em que a alma se despoja de todo apetite e caminha em pura fé, esperança e caridade rumo à união com Deus. Ficou inacabado."
  },
  "composed": "1578–1585",
  "languages": [
    "es-ES",
    "en-US",
    "pt-BR"
  ],
  "work": "john-of-the-cross/subida",
  "editions": {
    "es-ES": {
      "editor": "P. Silverio de Santa Teresa",
      "year": 1929
    },
    "en-US": {
      "translator": "David Lewis, revised by Benedict Zimmerman",
      "year": 1922
    }
  },
  "sources": [
    {
      "language": "es-ES",
      "url": "https://archive.org/details/obrasdesanjuande02john",
      "edition": "Obras de San Juan de la Cruz, Doctor de la Iglesia, ed. P. Silverio de Santa Teresa, C.D., t. II (Biblioteca Mística Carmelitana), Burgos: El Monte Carmelo, 1929, pp. 1–358. Princeton Theological Seminary scan.",
      "description": "Spanish critical text with Silverio's notes (manuscript variants, scripture references) kept as footnotes. OCR of the scan; page furniture removed; footnotes matched to their references page by page; OCR errors corrected by consulting P. Eulogio Pacho's modern text (Editorial Monte Carmelo, via Documenta Catholica Omnia), which was used only to find errors and never copied. Chapter summaries are taken from Silverio's own table of contents.",
      "tier": "A",
      "tierEvidence": "San Juan de la Cruz died in 1591. Silverio's edition was published in 1929 (before 1931: public domain in the US) and P. Silverio de Santa Teresa died in 1954, so his text and notes are public domain under life+70 since 1 January 2025. Caveat: Spain applies life+80 to authors who died before 1987, so in Spain alone his notes stay protected until 2035."
    },
    {
      "language": "en-US",
      "url": "https://archive.org/details/ascentofmountcar00johnuoft",
      "edition": "The Ascent of Mount Carmel, translated by David Lewis, with corrections and a prefatory essay by Benedict Zimmerman, O.C.D., 3rd ed., London: Thomas Baker, 1922. University of Toronto scan.",
      "description": "English translation with Lewis's scripture references as footnotes. Zimmerman's essay, the contents and the indexes are not included. Lewis's chapters follow the Spanish one for one, except that his 'Argument' of Book III is Silverio's chapter III.1, so his III.n is our l3-c(n+1).",
      "tier": "A",
      "tierEvidence": "Published 1922 (before 1931: public domain in the US); the translator David Lewis died in 1895 and the reviser Benedict Zimmerman in 1937, both more than 70 years ago."
    }
  ],
